            "review_title": "Review at Karaku Japanese Bbq",
            "review_text": "กษิดิศ\nThailand1 contribution\n3\nA cozy BBQ meal in Ho Chi Minh city\nNov 2024 • Family\nThis is a great Japanese-style restaurant. I'm currently on a trip to Ho Chi Minh City, Viet Nam and... This is the restaurant my Vietnamese friend recommended when I said I want to eat BBQ with a cozy space. I really love the food here. They have something called Yakiniku, which is very great with the original taste of the meat. Also there are some great corners to take pictures, my friends thought I was really in Japan after they saw my Instagram's story tho~ haha.\nSince I was having some health issues, I did not have some wine there but my father did. I don't really remember what he drank but it's the one has the sakura on the package. He said it's really matched with the food.\nOverall, I think I will come back to this restaurant in my next visit to Viet Nam.\nLove you all!\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nI think you guys must check the Koi fishes out, they are in the garden. Look pretty!\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 18, 2024",
