            "review_title": "Review at Karaku Japanese Bbq",
            "review_text": "Ivan\nCalifornia1 contribution\n3\nLunch Break Done Right at Karaku Japanese BBQ\nDec 2024 • Business\nMy team and I ditched the usual office lunch today and opted for some yakiniku at Karaku Japanese BBQ in Thu Duc. The ambiance was great – warm, inviting, and authentically Japanese. We snagged a semi-private spot, perfect for our group. I went for the Beef Belly set, and it was delicious! The beef was tender and flavorful, especially with their special sauce. Everyone in my team loved their sets too, from the Chicken Drumstick to the higher-end Beef Outside Skirt. There are some available dinks also; however, I realized that Karaku also had some special wine and many other alcoholic drinks too. But it was before our work time, so we did not have the chance to give it a try.\nOverall, Karaku is a fantastic spot for a quality and reasonably priced lunch. Definitely recommend!\n\nSmall tip for you guys: Book ahead if you want a private area, especially during peak hours.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nAsk for reservation in advance, so you can get a nice spot for check-in.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 17, 2024",
